# Core is read from the Ruby's own rbs, which can be older than the rbs the
# bundle declares. rbs polyfills `Module#ruby2_keywords` for Rubies without
# it, so the app's `ruby2_keywords` call credited rbs. A method the bundle's
# rbs describes under `core/` is core's, and credits no gem.
dead Gemfile rbs=unreferenced
